### 2. Core Modules & Engineering Scope

#### A. Land Acquisition & Due Diligence (Phase 1)

* **Title & Survey Registry:** Document repository with tamper-evident hashing (deed of assignment, governor’s consent, survey plans, C of O).
* **Zoning & Feasibility Tracking:** Pipeline tracker for environmental impact assessments, soil test uploads, and municipal permit clearance.
* **Escrow for Land Purchase:** Milestone-based milestone disbursement accounts between buyer and seller.

#### B. Construction Project Management (Phase 2)

* **Milestone & Budget Ledger:** Bill of Quantities (BOQ) tracking against real disbursements.
* **Vendor & Subcontractor Management:** RFQ submissions, bids, and purchase order tracking.
* **Field Inspection & Proof of Work:** Field engineer mobile interface with geofenced photo/video uploads to trigger milestone approvals before funds release.

#### C. Facility Management & Tenancy (Phase 3)

* **Tenant Lifecycle:** Digital leasing, auto-debit rent collection, utility bill breakdown, and move-in/move-out inspections.
* **Work Order & Maintenance Desk:** Ticketing engine for plumbing, electrical, HVAC, and civil repairs with vendor dispatch.
* **IoT / Utility Integration:** Metering data capture for power/water automation and energy consumption reports.

#### D. Real World Asset (RWA) Tokenization Layer

* **Legal-to-Code Mapping (SPV Architecture):** Each physical property must map to an off-chain Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV) holding the legal title. The token represents fractional equity or debt/yield shares in that SPV.
* **Smart Contract Standards:**
* ERC-3643 (T-REX) or ERC-1400 (Security Token Standards) rather than standard ERC-20, because real estate securities require on-chain compliance (permissioned transfers, whitelisted wallets, jurisdiction blocks).


* **Identity & Compliance (KYC/AML):** Integrated identity layer (e.g., Sumsub, Persona) linked to wallet whitelists before any buy/transfer transactions execute.
* **Rental Yield Distribution:** Automated smart contract distribution converting gross collected rent into net distribution (minus management fees, reserve fund, and taxes) credited directly to token holders' custodial or self-custody wallets.

